            {
                "entry_id": "0c0888bc-d934-321b-9047-ace47eecb268",
                "word": "putto",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e5241e14-6c86-4262-baa1-5157fd5d9c5f",
                        "entry_id": "0c0888bc-d934-321b-9047-ace47eecb268",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "puttos"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "59dcb44d-dc0e-4bb8-871d-04a0a9cec0f8",
                        "entry_id": "0c0888bc-d934-321b-9047-ace47eecb268",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular"
                        ],
                        "form": "putti"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d67cb8d3-d468-35bb-b1a8-39382df41730",
                        "entry_id": "0c0888bc-d934-321b-9047-ace47eecb268",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Petit enfant nu, parfois ailé, dans les représentations artistiques, souvent allégorie de l’amour."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b9c3252-ec1f-464e-b19a-5dd5bf80d1dd",
                                "sense_id": "d67cb8d3-d468-35bb-b1a8-39382df41730",
                                "text": "Notons qu’il existe, entre les deux races, quelques exemples d’un type mixte : voici un putto couronné de lierre dont la tête fait penser à celle d’un satyreau, ou, mieux encore, un putto sur le point de se métamorphoser en satyreau, […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ba86f29-21b7-4a38-8806-ae0a9d0169e5",
                                "sense_id": "d67cb8d3-d468-35bb-b1a8-39382df41730",
                                "text": "On lui reprochera d’avoir travaillé pour l’industrie, ainsi que ses œuvres jugées trop gracieuses où les putti abondent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0caeeba7-ae05-4778-9bfd-6919aaafacc9",
                        "source_entry_id": "0c0888bc-d934-321b-9047-ace47eecb268",
                        "source_sense_id": "d67cb8d3-d468-35bb-b1a8-39382df41730",
                        "target_lang_word": "Putto",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Putto",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63084c5c-2f3a-39f2-9258-a8a5fd50b874",
                                        "entry_id": "efe74934-d4fb-3123-be98-cee83b82d75d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "die Bezeichnung für die Figur eines kleinen nackten Knaben"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Kunstgeschichte"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2e25281-5507-4dd2-8abc-3b5dbbaa8e73",
                                                "sense_id": "63084c5c-2f3a-39f2-9258-a8a5fd50b874",
                                                "text": "Schon in der frühchristlichen Kunst gab es Putti."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a4375068-34e7-45cd-850b-af04c04490be",
                        "source_entry_id": "0c0888bc-d934-321b-9047-ace47eecb268",
                        "source_sense_id": "d67cb8d3-d468-35bb-b1a8-39382df41730",
                        "target_lang_word": "putto",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "putto",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6acde49-e441-39c2-ace9-7bf0f289c1ec",
                                        "entry_id": "a032586d-55fa-3cb9-a0da-df958c3767ae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A representation, especially in Renaissance or Baroque art, of a small, naked, often winged (usually male) child; a cherub."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97538c84-35c8-448b-aade-799562f434ea",
                                                "sense_id": "a6acde49-e441-39c2-ace9-7bf0f289c1ec",
                                                "text": "There is in the porch of the present church a tablet to Luke Flood (died 1818) which has much the appearance of having been made up of portions of earlier monuments. It is surmounted by a bas-relief of a winged boy holding an inverted torch. But not only is he a baby putto, not a youth, and without an urn, but the style and execution scarcely seem worthy of [Thomas] Banks even when not at his best."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8288c3c1-c832-43e4-9d04-1da3360e7e67",
                                                "sense_id": "a6acde49-e441-39c2-ace9-7bf0f289c1ec",
                                                "text": "The Carmelite scapulars held by the putto and young male saint on the right indicate that the altarpiece was intended for a church of the Carmelite order."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "204054b8-200b-4628-9910-10a019148f6f",
                                                "sense_id": "a6acde49-e441-39c2-ace9-7bf0f289c1ec",
                                                "text": "A second putto with a gallows in its hand cries at the judge's feet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9bef66b-cc5c-4c0c-8784-eb95ccfe0c0e",
                                                "sense_id": "a6acde49-e441-39c2-ace9-7bf0f289c1ec",
                                                "text": "In The Youth of Bacchus (illus. 51) [by Nicolas Poussin], a painting produced before 1630, the figures are arranged in a triangle. The young Bacchus is at the top, the putti lying on the ground and the feet of the sitting figures mark the base-line and the lower corner, while the sides are designated by the nymphs and satyrs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b939757-5ebf-4bd3-a648-ec5fab363d21",
                                                "sense_id": "a6acde49-e441-39c2-ace9-7bf0f289c1ec",
                                                "text": "The picture shows a putto who has just blown bubbles through a clay tube. He holds a scallop shell of soapy water and leans against a skull. [...] In picture and verse the imagery echoes classical and biblical metaphors for the brevity of a man's life. The fresh flower is in contrast to the dying tree like the putto as childhood innocence is opposed by the death's head."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58534a6a-6960-4568-b051-82a8ce3b610d",
                                                "sense_id": "a6acde49-e441-39c2-ace9-7bf0f289c1ec",
                                                "text": "The walls [of Naples Cathedral] have ranks of white marble niches capped by huge marble scallops, and flanked by urns and flowers, drapes and putti."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a91b8523-e8e5-4d80-b113-046a47e689fe",
                                                "sense_id": "a6acde49-e441-39c2-ace9-7bf0f289c1ec",
                                                "text": "Whatever the case, the evangelical animals are appreciably larger than the puttos of the painting. The animals gaze upward, their mouths gaping. They are cawing, bellowing, roaring out the Gospel. [...] Only the attendant puttos seem to be taking the divine afflatus or descent in stride."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b197da1-3062-44b3-9bd1-942ee6beb759",
                                                "sense_id": "a6acde49-e441-39c2-ace9-7bf0f289c1ec",
                                                "text": "A Galatea with Triton, 5 puttoes and 5 other figures, painted frame in fake marble and gilded, 12 palmi in height, copy of Raphael made by Caracci."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
